<Project>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MinVer" Version="6.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Test projects only, and deliberately not the shipping ones.

    ITfoxtec.Identity.Saml2 asks for System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 10.0.7, which carries five
    high-severity advisories. The applications never resolve it: the ASP.NET Core shared framework
    supersedes that package, so Connapse.Web's dependency graph has no entry for it and the
    published output ships no copy — the assembly comes from whatever runtime the container has.
    A test assembly is a plain library with no shared framework behind it, so there the package
    materialises for real, at 10.0.7, and NU1903 fires on every build.

    Pinned here rather than in each test project because the reason is the same for all of them,
    and at the version Connapse.Storage already pins for its own copy, so the repository carries
    one number instead of two. Do NOT add this to a project under src/: a direct reference would
    make an application ship its own copy of an assembly the framework already supplies, which is
    a copy somebody then has to keep patched.

    Remove once ITfoxtec.Identity.Saml2 asks for a patched version.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="$(MSBuildProjectName.EndsWith('.Tests'))">
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" Version="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- MinVer reads git tags like "v0.3.2" to set the version automatically.
         Push a higher tag to bump the version. Untagged commits get a pre-release suffix. -->
    <MinVerTagPrefix>v</MinVerTagPrefix>
    <MinVerDefaultPreReleaseIdentifiers>alpha.0</MinVerDefaultPreReleaseIdentifiers>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
